  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The correct order of reagents for the following reaction is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>MgBr</mi></math>&nbsp;&amp; the reaction as well as mechanism is as follows with the correct order of reagents.</p><p>The reaction involves&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SN</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;mechanism at second step which on further reaction with excess&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>MgBr</mi></math>&nbsp;to give the final product.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e18fe0e9-d54d-4d5d-94af-83e2cfcfaa19-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 400px;\" /><br /><br />&nbsp;</p>",
